// incident_acks (app-spec §9.1, §9.6; ADR-001 Decision 1) — the admin
// acknowledgment of an indexer-computed incident.
//
// It lives in `app` and not beside `incidents` because the two have different
// owners: incidents are computed facts the indexer writes, the acknowledgment
// is an app action. The web tier NEVER writes `incidents` — `app_writer` holds
// no grants on `indexed` at all (roles.sql; the standing grant-boundary gate).
// The reference is BY ID with no cross-schema foreign key, because there are
// none across the domain boundary; validity is established by reading the
// incident live at write time, not by the database.
//
// KEY (plan §4b C1, resolved 2026-07-31). A surrogate `id`, plus a PARTIAL
// unique index on (incidentId, acknowledgedBy) WHERE unacknowledgedAt IS NULL,
// hand-written in the migration because Prisma cannot express a partial unique
// index. `incidentId` alone is the obvious key and is wrong the moment two
// admins acknowledge, or one re-acknowledges after a reversal: later writes
// would silently overwrite earlier ones, which is how batched payments were
// lost. The constraint is also the CONCURRENCY remedy (C3) — two admins racing
// are separated by the database, never by an application-level "already acked?"
// read-then-write.
//
// REVERSAL PRESERVES HISTORY: un-acknowledging sets `unacknowledgedAt` rather
// than deleting the row, so the audit trail survives and the partial index
// frees the pair for a fresh ack.
//
// Columns are gated by test/app-schema-allowlist.test.ts. `acknowledgedBy` is a
// bech32 wallet address (public chain data, and the SESSION address only —
// never a client-supplied actor); the timestamps are operational metadata; and
// `note` is the one judgement call, taken deliberately at plan §7 Q2 (Ira,
// 2026-07-31): operator text ABOUT AN INCIDENT, not about a person, bounded at
// 500 characters so it cannot become an unbounded free-text column in the one
// schema that is not rebuildable from chain.

model IncidentAck {
  id               BigInt    @id @default(autoincrement())
  /** `indexed.incidents.id`. No cross-schema FK exists (ADR-001 Decision 1);
   * the id is validated against a live read of the incident on write. */
  incidentId       Int
  /** bech32 address of the acknowledging admin — the SESSION address (public
   * chain data). Never a client-supplied actor. */
  acknowledgedBy   String
  acknowledgedAt   DateTime  @default(now())
  /** Set on reversal; the row is kept so the trail is not lost. NULL means
   * this is the LIVE ack, which is what the partial unique index keys on. */
  unacknowledgedAt DateTime?
  /** Optional bounded operator note about the incident (§7 Q2). */
  note             String?   @db.VarChar(500)

  @@index([incidentId])
  @@map("incident_acks")
  @@schema("app")
}
